WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:01.886
- [Voiceover] Let's say
that we have an exponential

00:01.886 --> 00:03.116
function, h of n,

00:03.116 --> 00:04.625
and since it's an exponential function

00:04.625 --> 00:07.830
it's going to be in the
form a times r to the n,

00:07.830 --> 00:09.339
where a is our initial value

00:09.339 --> 00:10.648
and r is our common ratio,

00:10.648 --> 00:13.147
and we're going to assume
that r is greater than zero.

00:13.147 --> 00:15.631
And they've given us some
information on h of n.

00:15.631 --> 00:17.373
We know that when n is equal to 2,

00:17.373 --> 00:19.393
h of 2 is 144,

00:19.393 --> 00:21.599
that h of 4 is 324,

00:21.599 --> 00:24.710
that h of 6 is 729.

00:24.710 --> 00:26.498
So, based on the information here,

00:26.498 --> 00:27.984
let's see if we can actually figure out

00:27.984 --> 00:31.142
what a and r are going to be.

00:31.142 --> 00:34.833
And like always, pause the
video and try to give it a go.

00:34.833 --> 00:36.737
All right, now let's do this together.

00:36.737 --> 00:39.384
So I'm going to focus on r first.

00:39.384 --> 00:41.706
The common ratio

00:41.706 --> 00:44.910
and if we had successive n's.

00:44.910 --> 00:47.836
If we had h of 3, then
we could just find the

00:47.836 --> 00:50.460
ratio between h of 3 and h of 2

00:50.460 --> 00:52.294
and r would just come out of that,

00:52.294 --> 00:55.150
or if the ratio between h of 4 and h of 3,

00:55.150 --> 00:56.938
we could solve explicitly for r,

00:56.938 --> 00:58.517
but we can get pretty close to that.

00:58.517 --> 01:00.630
We can just find the ratio between h of 4

01:00.630 --> 01:01.907
and h of 2.

01:01.907 --> 01:04.229
So, h of 4,

01:04.229 --> 01:05.854
the ratio between h of 4

01:05.854 --> 01:07.595
and h of 2

01:07.595 --> 01:09.615
is going to be equal to,

01:09.615 --> 01:13.075
well, we know h of 4 is 324,

01:13.075 --> 01:15.977
and h of 2 is 144,

01:15.977 --> 01:18.578
and we could simplify this a little bit.

01:18.578 --> 01:20.691
Let's see, if we,

01:20.691 --> 01:23.245
if we simplify this, we would get,

01:23.245 --> 01:24.499
they're both divisible by 2.

01:24.499 --> 01:25.985
If we divide them both by 2,

01:25.985 --> 01:27.308
this one in the numerator,

01:27.308 --> 01:30.721
324 divided by 2 is 162.

01:30.721 --> 01:33.624
144 divided by 2 is 72.

01:33.624 --> 01:35.621
Let's see, we can divide by 2 again.

01:35.621 --> 01:38.430
81 over 36.

01:38.430 --> 01:39.289
Divide by 2,

01:39.289 --> 01:41.100
actually, no, we can't
divide by 2 anymore,

01:41.100 --> 01:42.865
but we can divide by 9 now,

01:42.865 --> 01:46.000
so 81 divided by 9 is 9,

01:46.000 --> 01:48.113
and 36 divided by 9 is 4.

01:48.113 --> 01:51.897
So this thing can be rewritten as 9/4,

01:51.897 --> 01:54.405
but we could also rewrite this ratio

01:54.405 --> 01:55.519
by using,

01:55.519 --> 01:58.700
using this form of an
exponential function,

01:58.700 --> 02:01.254
so we could also say that
this is going to be equal to,

02:01.254 --> 02:03.367
h of 4 is going to be a

02:03.367 --> 02:04.993
times r.

02:04.993 --> 02:07.616
Now n is 4, so r to the 4th power,

02:07.616 --> 02:11.842
and h of 2 is going to be
a times r to the 2nd power.

02:11.842 --> 02:15.070
A times r to the 2nd power,

02:15.070 --> 02:16.695
and this simplifies nicely,

02:16.695 --> 02:18.274
a divided by a,

02:18.274 --> 02:19.690
cancels to just 1,

02:19.690 --> 02:22.500
and r to the 4th divided by r-squared,

02:22.500 --> 02:24.613
well that's going to be
r to the 4 minus 2 power,

02:24.613 --> 02:25.402
or r,

02:25.402 --> 02:26.981
it's going to be r to the 2nd power,

02:26.981 --> 02:29.024
it's going to be r-squared,

02:29.024 --> 02:30.812
and so we have a nice
little equation set up.

02:30.812 --> 02:35.061
R-squared needs to be equal to 9/4.

02:35.061 --> 02:36.083
So let me write that down.

02:36.083 --> 02:38.382
R-squared is equal to 9/4,

02:38.382 --> 02:40.587
and r needs to be greater than zero,

02:40.587 --> 02:43.536
so we could just say r is
going to be the principal root

02:43.536 --> 02:45.719
of 9/4,

02:45.719 --> 02:48.528
which is equal to 3/2.

02:48.528 --> 02:51.315
So we were able to figure out r.

02:51.315 --> 02:53.056
So now how do we figure out,

02:53.056 --> 02:55.378
how do we figure out a?

02:55.378 --> 02:56.980
Well, there's a couple of ways to do it.

02:56.980 --> 03:00.533
You can think about a is
going to be what h of zero

03:00.533 --> 03:01.392
is equal to,

03:01.392 --> 03:02.274
so we could do,

03:02.274 --> 03:04.758
I guess we could call it a tabular method,

03:04.758 --> 03:06.709
where, let me set up

03:06.709 --> 03:08.984
a little table here.

03:08.984 --> 03:10.540
So, a little table,

03:10.540 --> 03:14.510
so if this is n and this is h of n,

03:14.510 --> 03:15.857
so n is zero,

03:15.857 --> 03:17.529
we don't know what h of zero is just yet,

03:17.529 --> 03:18.574
it's going to be a.

03:18.574 --> 03:22.149
We don't know what h of 1 is yet.

03:22.149 --> 03:26.352
We do know that h of 2 is 144.

03:26.352 --> 03:29.162
And we do know, since
the common ratio is 3/2,

03:29.162 --> 03:33.179
if we take h of 1 and
we multiply it by 3/2,

03:33.179 --> 03:35.175
we're going to get h of 2,

03:35.175 --> 03:38.240
and if we take h of zero
and multiply it by 3/2,

03:38.240 --> 03:40.701
we're going to get h of 1.

03:40.701 --> 03:45.136
So, h of 1 is going to
be 144 divided by 3/2.

03:45.136 --> 03:45.949
So let's write that down.

03:45.949 --> 03:49.246
H of 1 is equal to 144

03:49.246 --> 03:52.450
divided by 3/2,

03:52.450 --> 03:56.165
which is going to be 144,

03:56.165 --> 04:00.530
144 times 2 over 3,

04:00.530 --> 04:01.297
and let's see,

04:01.297 --> 04:05.639
144 divided by 3 is

04:05.639 --> 04:08.170
going to be equal to,

04:08.170 --> 04:09.330
is it,

04:09.330 --> 04:09.841
let's see,

04:09.841 --> 04:11.699
one 3 goes into,

04:11.699 --> 04:12.535
I'll just do this by hand,

04:12.535 --> 04:14.276
my brain doesn't work that well

04:14.276 --> 04:15.460
while I'm making videos.

04:15.460 --> 04:18.502
3 goes into 14 four times,

04:18.502 --> 04:19.756
4 times 3 is 12,

04:19.756 --> 04:20.731
subtract,

04:20.731 --> 04:22.147
so it's going to be,

04:22.147 --> 04:24.372
I see, it's going to be 48.

04:24.372 --> 04:26.113
3 goes into 24 eight times.

04:26.113 --> 04:27.274
8 times 3 is 24,

04:27.274 --> 04:28.899
you have no remainder,

04:28.899 --> 04:30.455
so,

04:30.455 --> 04:34.751
this is going to be 48 times 2,

04:34.751 --> 04:37.189
which is going to be equal to 96

04:37.189 --> 04:38.953
so this is going to be 96,

04:38.953 --> 04:40.602
and so if we want to figure out h of zero,

04:40.602 --> 04:42.831
we just divide by 3/2 again,

04:42.831 --> 04:46.778
so, h of zero is 96

04:46.778 --> 04:49.588
divided by 3/2

04:49.588 --> 04:54.046
which is equal to 96 times 2 over 3.

04:54.046 --> 04:56.507
96 divided by 3, let's see,

04:56.507 --> 04:57.900
it's going to be 32,

04:57.900 --> 05:01.290
so this is going to be 32

05:01.290 --> 05:03.124
times, did I do that right?

05:03.124 --> 05:04.680
Yup, 32 times 2

05:04.680 --> 05:07.513
which is equal to 64.

05:07.513 --> 05:08.975
64.

05:08.975 --> 05:10.740
And so, just like that,
we've figured out that a

05:10.740 --> 05:13.108
is equal to 64,

05:13.108 --> 05:15.059
and r,

05:15.059 --> 05:18.054
and r is equal to 3/2.

05:18.054 --> 05:20.097
So we can write h of n,

05:20.097 --> 05:24.648
we can say that h of n is equal to 64,

05:24.648 --> 05:28.061
is equal to 64

05:28.061 --> 05:30.982
times 3/2,

05:31.660 --> 05:33.657
times 3/2,

05:33.657 --> 05:34.934
our common ratio,

05:34.934 --> 05:37.117
to the nth power.

05:37.117 --> 05:38.858
Now, there's another way that
we could have tackled this

05:38.858 --> 05:40.484
instead of this tabular method.

05:40.484 --> 05:42.991
We could have just solved for a now,

05:42.991 --> 05:43.966
since we know r.

05:43.966 --> 05:45.777
We know, for example,

05:45.777 --> 05:49.237
we know for example that h of 2

05:49.237 --> 05:53.300
which is going to be equal to a times,

05:53.300 --> 05:55.088
we know what our common ratio is,

05:55.088 --> 05:56.969
it's 3/2

05:56.969 --> 05:59.361
to the 2nd power,

05:59.361 --> 06:03.424
is going to be equal to 144.

06:03.424 --> 06:07.603
And so, we could say a times 9 over 4

06:07.603 --> 06:10.297
is equal to 144,

06:10.297 --> 06:12.479
and so we can multiply both
sides times the reciprocal

06:12.479 --> 06:13.362
of 9 over 4,

06:13.362 --> 06:16.682
so we multiply both sides times 4 over 9,

06:16.682 --> 06:19.445
times 4 over 9,

06:19.445 --> 06:20.327
and that cancels with that,

06:20.327 --> 06:21.744
that cancels with that,

06:21.744 --> 06:23.671
and we are left with

06:23.671 --> 06:25.993
a is equal to, well let's see,

06:25.993 --> 06:29.174
144 divided by 9

06:29.174 --> 06:31.356
is going to be,

06:31.356 --> 06:35.559
is going to be, I want
to say it's equal to 16?

06:35.559 --> 06:37.997
Is that right?

06:37.997 --> 06:39.181
I think that is right.

06:39.181 --> 06:40.574
Yup, and then 16 times 4,

06:40.574 --> 06:43.453
so this is going to be 16 and 1,

06:43.453 --> 06:46.495
16 times 4 is 64,

06:46.495 --> 06:48.492
which is exactly what we got before,

06:48.492 --> 06:49.560
and so this actually,

06:49.560 --> 06:50.698
this method, now that I look at it,

06:50.698 --> 06:53.298
is actually a good bit easier,

06:53.298 --> 06:53.972
but they're equivalent,

06:53.972 --> 06:55.829
and I like this one because
you get to see the common

06:55.829 --> 06:58.499
ratio in action, and you get
to see that the initial value

06:58.499 --> 06:59.776
is the initial value.

06:59.776 --> 07:01.541
It is h of zero,

07:01.541 --> 07:02.470
but either way,

07:02.470 --> 07:03.445
once you figure out r,

07:03.445 --> 07:05.860
and you know one of the

07:05.860 --> 07:06.765
h of,

07:06.765 --> 07:08.855
you know what the function is at a value,

07:08.855 --> 07:10.271
you can solve for a,

07:10.271 --> 07:11.711
and frankly, if you
knew a and you knew what

07:11.711 --> 07:13.104
the function was for a given n,

07:13.104 --> 07:15.983
